(a) The city may permit parks and park facilities to be reserved for use at a particular time, subject to the procedures, rules and regulations, conditions and requirements for reservation of facilities that may be established and approved from time to time by the city manager.
(b) In the absence of reservations, the use of any park or park facilities shall be on a first come-first served basis.
(c) Athletic fields within any parks shall be reserved for organized competition and/or practice in accordance with the rules and regulations established and maintained by the city or the city's designee and shall only be used for organized competition and/or practice pursuant to a reservation made in accordance with the rules and regulations established by the city or the city's designee.
(d) Park facilities are intended for the use of the general public for recreational purposes, such as picnicking, exercise, use of playground equipment, nature study, and similar activities on an informal basis. A park use permit shall be required for organized group activities, included but not limited to concerts and performances, and for uses that otherwise would not be allowed by this chapter or any rules or regulations promulgated hereunder. The city may maintain a list of activities that require a park use permit, which list may be updated from time-to-time by the city manager or the designee of the city manager at the direction of the city manager.
(e) A park use permit may be issued by the city manager or the designee of the city manager, taking into consideration the following:
(1) The facilities requested have not been reserved for other use on the date and time period requested in the application and that the proposed activity will not otherwise conflict with existing park activities and services;
(2) That adequate sanitary facilities will be provided;
(3) That appropriate safety precautions will be taken and as may be required in connection with issuance of the permit;
(4) That the activity will not unreasonably interfere with the use of the park and neighboring property by others and will not unreasonably interfere with or detract from the promotion of public health, welfare, safety and recreation;
(5) That there will be adequate security against damages to the city or the property of the city, including but not limited to the requirement that the applicant agree to indemnify and hold harmless the city and/or provide liability insurance naming the city as an additional insured, as may be reasonably required in consideration of the facts and circumstances surrounding the proposed activity;
(6) That the proposed activity will not entail extraordinary or burdensome expense or police operations or protection by the city;
(7) That the proposed activity or use of the park or recreation facility is not reasonably anticipated to incite violence, crime, or disorderly conduct; and
(8) That the proposed activity will comply with the requirements of this chapter, this Code, and all applicable rules and regulations adopted thereto, and all other state and local laws.
(f) An application for a park use permit shall be made on the forms and according to the guidelines provided by the city. The application shall be accompanied by the necessary fees and information specified in this chapter and by rules and regulations made pursuant to this chapter.
(g) The city may charge a fee for use of a park or park facility, or for a park use permit. Such fees shall be set by the city council and maintained in the office of the city clerk.
(h) The city manager or the city manager's designee shall have the authority to revoke any park use permit upon finding of any material misrepresentation made in any application for a park use permit, any violations of conditions placed upon the issuance of any park use permit, any violation of this chapter, any rules and regulations made pursuant to this chapter, this Code, any state or local laws, or upon any other good cause shown.
(i) The city manager, or the city manager's designee shall have the authority to cancel an activity for which a park use permit has been issued due to special circumstances, including but not limited to inclement weather.
(j) The city manager, or the city manager's designee, shall have the authority to order any person or persons acting in violation of this chapter, any rules and regulations made pursuant to this chapter, any conditions placed upon the issuance of any park use permit, this Code, any state or local laws, or upon any other good cause shown.
(Ord. No. 10-05282024, § I, 5-28-2024)
